    "summary": "Man’s cloth (Asante kente), composed of 30 strips hand-woven from imported cotton and rayon, and hand-sewn together along the selvedges. The warp pattern in identical in all the strips, and is formed of lines of red, black, yellow, green and white thread. The ground weft is red. An extremely complex pattern is formed by blocks of supplementary weft placed in chequerboard fashion across the centre of the cloth; the two ends have six continuous bands of a different pattern. The warp ends have been left as a fringe.",
